  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES.\n\nRepro re-run: the parity CASES[\"dart\"] fixture through run_behavior_map emits class Shape, class Square,\nmethod Shape.area, method Square.area, the file node, and 4 contains edges -- no extends/implements/\ninherits, no dispatches_to. Premise holds as written.\n- packages/hypergumbo-lang-common/src/hypergumbo_lang_common/dart.py (1158 lines): no reference to\n  superclass/interfaces/implements/extends/base_classes. Only commits since filing: f251ea5bbc, 509ec58cc7\n  (both unrelated).\n- tests/test_interface_dispatch_parity.py:130 still holds KNOWN_HOLES[\"dart\"] naming this item.\n\nUPDATES / scoping the fix (not in the description):\n1. The shared producer is linkers/inheritance.py, which mints extends/implements edges from Symbol.meta\n   \"base_classes\" (META-001). The fix is for dart.py to WRITE meta[\"base_classes\"] (superclass +\n   interfaces + with-mixins), not to emit edges itself. inheritance.py:550-556 already says\n   \"dart/elixir write neither key\"; adding \"dart\" to that linker's depends_on is part of the same change.\n2. Dart `abstract class Shape` is emitted with modifiers=[] (no \"abstract\"). Not needed for dispatch\n   (dart is not in NO_VIRTUAL_EXTENDS_LANGUAGES, so an extends edge is admitted), but worth noting if\n   anything downstream keys on is_abstract_type.\n3. inherited_calls.py:565 and :875 also note \"dart ... emit no inheritance model\" -- a second consumer\n   that would light up once base_classes is written.\nNot checked: a real Dart corpus (the dead-code consequence remains unmeasured, as the item says).\nRelated: WI-kalug (TS interface-extends-interface emits zero inheritance edges), WI-sujon (dart ctors)."  # 4fae
