    description: "**Measured** by the interface-dispatch parity column (`test_interface_dispatch_parity.py`), on:\n\n    abstract class Shape { int area(); }\n    class Square implements Shape { int area() => 1; }\n\nThe analyzer emits **all four symbols correctly**, with dot-qualified member names that every shared linker can parse:\n\n    class   'Shape'         method  'Shape.area'\n    class   'Square'        method  'Square.area'\n\nand **no inheritance edge whatsoever** — no `implements`, no `extends`, no `inherits`. So `linkers/type_hierarchy` has nothing to build its inheritance maps from and Dart gets no `dispatches_to` edge.\n\nThis is the cleanest of the parity column's four remaining holes (cpp, kotlin, dart, elixir): nothing about naming, nothing about vocabulary, nothing about kinds. One missing producer emission.\n\n**Fix path.** Edges are not minted by analyzers here: `linkers/inheritance.py` (the shared producer, META-001) builds `extends`/`implements` edges from `Symbol.meta[\"base_classes\"]`, and its `depends_on` comment already records \"dart/elixir write neither key\". `packages/hypergumbo-lang-common/src/hypergumbo_lang_common/dart.py` contains no superclass/interfaces/`base_classes` handling at all. So the fix is for `dart.py` to write `meta[\"base_classes\"]` (superclass, `implements` list, `with` mixins) and for `dart` to join that linker's `depends_on` — not to emit edges in the analyzer. `linkers/inherited_calls.py` also notes dart has no inheritance model, so it is a second consumer that lights up.\n\nNote: `abstract class Shape` is emitted with `modifiers=[]` (no `abstract`). Dart is not in `NO_VIRTUAL_EXTENDS_LANGUAGES`, so this does not block dispatch, but anything keyed on `is_abstract_type` will not see it.\n\n**Consequence beyond dispatch.** `implements`/`extends` edges feed inheritance-based reachability, so a Dart class that is only ever used through its interface reads as dead code. Not measured on a real Dart corpus — quantifying it is the first step of the fix, not a claim being made here.\n\nHole recorded as a strict xfail (`KNOWN_HOLES[\"dart\"]`); fixing the analyzer XPASSes the cell and forces the entry's removal in the same PR.\n\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # f987
- op: discuss  # d99a
  at: '2026-10-01T17:46:29Z'  # d99a
  by: agent  # d99a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d99a
  clock: 4  # d99a
  nonce: d99a  # d99a
  message: "IMPLEMENTED on local branch `jgstern-agent/fix/lahub` (worktree ~/hg_wt/lahub; not pushed). Commits: e650e446fc (fix) and 55c96deda0 (docs). Full report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_09302026/lahub.md.\n\nThe item's suggested route (dart.py writes meta.base_classes, linkers/inheritance.py builds the edges) was NOT taken. That linker labels an edge by its TARGET's kind, and Dart has no interface kind, so every Dart `implements` would have become `extends`. Its maps also index no `mixin` kind, so `with` would be dropped. Instead, the Dart analyzer records each class/mixin/enum's heritage clauses in Pass 1 (matched to the symbol by position) and resolves them in post_process:\n- `extends` gives extends.\n- `implements` gives implements.\n- `with` gives includes/ast_includes.\n- A mixin's `on` gives extends.\nResolution order: the same-file candidate, else the only candidate, else an INV-zuhub fallback (confidence 0.5 plus the flag). A base with no candidate becomes `dart:external:0-0:<Name>:unresolved`. `dart` was added to type-hierarchy-linker.depends_on and to INHERITANCE_EDGE_TYPE_LANGUAGES. KNOWN_HOLES[\"dart\"] was removed from the parity column. inheritance.py is untouched.\n\nEvidence:\n- New test_dart_inheritance.py (17 tests): red on the unfixed code (13 failed, 3 negative controls passed), green after the fix.\n- Targeted smart-test on HEAD: 14151 passed, 2 skipped, 4 xfailed; 100% coverage on changed files.\n- The parity dart cell is a hard pass, and run_behavior_map gives `Shape.area -dispatches_to-> Square.area`.\n- sherpa-onnx survey: Dart `extends` went 0 -> 105, all to external bases (Struct/Opaque/Flutter). No other edge type changed count, and Dart dispatches_to stayed 0 -> 0 because the repo has no in-tree Dart inheritance.\n\nResiduals filed (P3):\n- WI-riroz-masam-minaf-tivid-foruf-bokih-fudit-zuzuk: Dart MRO walker.\n- WI-volus-hidar-folod-hanoz-kumam-bahik-hogop-josad: mixin application class and extension type emit no symbol.\n- WI-sokin-valik-kahuf-pavub-nukoh-guzov-kakir-fodaz: the grammar swallows classes that have `external` fields.\n- WI-nakur-muhov-nisad-mapol-tunis-zipuh-vabaf-nijik: the producer-set scanner is blind to a non-literal edge_type.\n\nNo status change made."  # d99a
